<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation" xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml" xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib">

    <!--  Connection Options Dialog Tooltips  -->
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.ComputerName">Computer Name, IP address or the namespace path (e.g. \\remotepc\root\default) to connect to (leave empty for local machine).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.Username">Set the user name to be used for the connection operation (leave empty for current user).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.Password">Set the password for the specified user.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.EnablePrivileges">Specify whether user privileges need to be enabled for the connection operation. This property should only be used when the operation performed requires a certain user privilege to be enabled (for example, a machine restart).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.AuthenticationLevel">Set the COM authentication level to be used for operatoins in this connection.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.ImpersonationLevel">Set the COM impersonation level to be used for operations in this connection.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.Authority">Set the Authority (e.g., kerberos:&lt;DOMAIN&gt; or ntlmdomain:&lt;DOMAIN&gt;) to authenticate the specified user.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.Timeout">Set the time-out to apply to the operation.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.Locale">Set the Locale to be used for the connection operation (e.g., 'MS_409' for English US). Leave empty for system default.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.EditContext">Enable editing of WMI context object. This is a name-value pairs list to be passed through to a WMI provider that supports context information for customized operation.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.ContextKey">Enter the context key name</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.ContextValue">Enter the context value</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.AddContext">Add the key-value pair to the context</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.RemoveContext">Remove</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.ClearContext">Clear all context items</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.ConnectionOptions.Reset">Reset all options to default values</sys:String>

    <!--  Watcher Tab Tooltips  -->
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.Start">Start</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.Stop">Stop</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.Remove">Remove</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.EventType">Select the type of WMI event to monitor (e.g., __InstanceCreationEvent, __InstanceModificationEvent, __InstanceDeletionEvent).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.Within">Specify the polling interval in seconds for events. Lower values provide more responsive monitoring but consume more resources.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.EventProperty">Select a property from the event class to monitor for specific changes or conditions.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.EventPropertyValue">Optional: Specify a value to filter events by. Only events where the selected property matches this value will be captured.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.TargetClass">Specify the WMI class to monitor for events (e.g., Win32_Process, Win32_Service). This determines what objects the watcher will observe.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.TargetClassProperty">Optional: Select a specific property of the target class to monitor. Useful for filtering events based on property changes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.TargetClassPropertyValue">Optional: Specify a value to filter target class events by. Only events affecting objects with this property value will be captured.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.EventDisplayProperty">Choose which property value to display in the events list for easy identification of captured events.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.CustomQuery">Enable this to write a custom WQL event query instead of using the query builder. Provides full control over the event subscription.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.EventQuery">The WQL event query that will be executed. When Custom is unchecked, this is automatically generated from the builder options above.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.AddWatcher">Create a new event watcher with the current query configuration. The watcher will be added to the list and started automatically.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.StartAll">Start all event watchers in the list simultaneously. Active watchers will begin monitoring for events immediately.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.StopAll">Stop all currently running event watchers. This pauses event monitoring but preserves the watcher configurations.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.RemoveAll">Remove all event watchers from the list. This will stop any running watchers and clear the entire watcher configuration.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.WatchersList">List of configured event watchers. Shows the state, name, query, and namespace for each watcher. Use the action buttons to control individual watchers.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.WatcherFilter">Filter the events list by watcher name.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.ClearEvents">Clear all captured events from the events list. This does not affect the watchers themselves, only the displayed event history.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.FilterEvents">Filter the events list by typing text to search for in any column. Use this to quickly find specific events in large event logs.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Watcher.EventsList">List of events captured by the active watchers. Shows timestamp, display property values, and source watcher information for each event.</sys:String>

    <!--  Query Tab Tooltips  -->
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Query.DirectAccess">Sets a value indicating whether direct access to the WMI provider is requested for the specified class, without any regard to its super class or derived classes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Query.UseAmendedQualifiers">Sets a value indicating whether the objects returned from WMI should contain amended information. Typically, amended information is localizable information attached to the WMI object, such as object and property descriptions.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Query.QueryEditor">Enter your WQL (WMI Query Language) query here. Use Ctrl+Space for auto-completion of class names and properties.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Query.Execute">Execute the WQL query against the selected WMI namespace. Results will be displayed in the grid below.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Query.Cancel">Cancel the currently running query operation.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Query.FilterResults">Filter the query results by typing text to search for in any column. The filter is applied in real-time.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Query.ClearResults">Clear all query results from the grid and reset the view.</sys:String>

    <!--  Common UI Tooltips  -->
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Common.Clear">Clear</sys:String>

    <!--  Options View Tooltips  -->
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Options.ComputerName">Enter the computer name, IP address, or namespace path (e.g., \\remotepc\root\default) to connect to. Leave empty for the local machine.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Options.Connect">Connect to the specified computer using the current connection settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Options.ConnectionOptions">Open advanced connection options dialog to configure authentication, timeouts, and other connection parameters.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Options.AsynchronousMode">Use asynchronous WMI operations with ManagementOperationObserver. Provides real-time progress updates and immediate cancellation support through the WMI API.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Options.SynchronousMode">Use synchronous WMI operations with timeout-based cancellation (30s by default, 60s for queries/instances). Operations are wrapped in tasks to prevent UI blocking and can be cancelled via timeout or cancellation token.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Options.IncludeCimClasses">Include Common Information Model (CIM) classes in the class enumeration. These are standard WMI classes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Options.IncludeMsftClasses">Include Microsoft-specific (MSFT) classes in the class enumeration. These are vendor-specific WMI classes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Options.IncludePerfClasses">Include Performance Counter (Perf) classes in the class enumeration. These classes provide system performance data.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Options.ReloadClasses">Refresh and reload the WMI class list from the connected computer with the current filter settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Options.PrimaryAccentColor">Select the primary accent color for the application theme. This color is used for highlights and primary UI elements.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.Options.SecondaryAccentColor">Select the secondary accent color for the application theme. This color is used for secondary UI elements and complementary highlights.</sys:String>

</ResourceDictionary>
